{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"d51b043006f055e2","name":"card_unit_fifth_ohio","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_fifth_ohio","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FIFTH OHIO","text":"Deployment: Destroy target enemy unit with combined attack and defense of 6 or less.","flavorText":"The Fifth Ohio, officially called 145th Infantry Regiment, entered federal service in 1940 with the 37th Infantry Division of the US Army, later known as the Buckeye Division. After training at Camp Shelby and taking part in the Louisiana Maneuvers, the regiment sailed to Fiji in 1942, before entering combat in the Solomon Islands. In New Georgia in 1943, the 145th fought in the Battle of Bairoko. Its troops moved through jungle, mud, and hidden Japanese defenses as Allied forces tried to cut supply routes to Munda. The fighting was slow and costly, with strong points often cleared one at a time. The regiment later fought on Bougainville, where the defense of Hill 700 became one of its hardest engagements. In 1945, the 145th joined the Luzon campaign. It helped take Clark Field, fought in Manila, and stormed intra muros through the Quezon and Parian Gates.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_fifth_ohio","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_fifth_ohio_title","SourceString":"FIFTH OHIO","LocalizedString":"FIFTH OHIO"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_fifth_ohio_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Destroy target enemy unit with combined attack and defense of 6 or less.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Destroy target enemy unit with combined attack and defense of 6 or less."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_fifth_ohio_history","SourceString":"The Fifth Ohio, officially called 145th Infantry Regiment, entered federal service in 1940 with the 37th Infantry Division of the US Army, later known as the Buckeye Division. After training at Camp Shelby and taking part in the Louisiana Maneuvers, the regiment sailed to Fiji in 1942, before entering combat in the Solomon Islands. In New Georgia in 1943, the 145th fought in the Battle of Bairoko. Its troops moved through jungle, mud, and hidden Japanese defenses as Allied forces tried to cut supply routes to Munda. The fighting was slow and costly, with strong points often cleared one at a time. The regiment later fought on Bougainville, where the defense of Hill 700 became one of its hardest engagements. In 1945, the 145th joined the Luzon campaign. It helped take Clark Field, fought in Manila, and stormed intra muros through the Quezon and Parian Gates.","LocalizedString":"The Fifth Ohio, officially called 145th Infantry Regiment, entered federal service in 1940 with the 37th Infantry Division of the US Army, later known as the Buckeye Division. After training at Camp Shelby and taking part in the Louisiana Maneuvers, the regiment sailed to Fiji in 1942, before entering combat in the Solomon Islands. In New Georgia in 1943, the 145th fought in the Battle of Bairoko. Its troops moved through jungle, mud, and hidden Japanese defenses as Allied forces tried to cut supply routes to Munda. The fighting was slow and costly, with strong points often cleared one at a time. The regiment later fought on Bougainville, where the defense of Hill 700 became one of its hardest engagements. In 1945, the 145th joined the Luzon campaign. It helped take Clark Field, fought in Manila, and stormed intra muros through the Quezon and Parian Gates."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","hasDeployment":true,"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FIFTH_OHIO.FIFTH_OHIO","SubPathString":""},"hist